WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.640
There are so many new beauty products

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.900
being released all the time,

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.555
so we gathered some of the most hyped

00:00:09.555 --> 00:00:11.900
from the last month to test for ourselves.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.719
I've been dying to try
out this Freck Cheekslime,

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:15.961
mainly because of the name,

00:00:15.961 --> 00:00:17.585
and I've been obsessed with all kinds

00:00:17.585 --> 00:00:19.150
of liquid blushes lately.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.330
I'll admit I went in too hot.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.090
I applied way too much too fast,

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.423
and I think the sponge

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:26.231
wasn't the best way to apply this.

00:00:26.231 --> 00:00:29.720
She was giving clown,
so we did a take two.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.430
I used less, and I went in with a brush,

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.980
and it worked out so much better.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.490
This stuff dries down super quickly,

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.530
so I recommend doing one cheek at a time,

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.370
but the color payoff is amazing.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.130
I don't think I like it
very much as a lip tint.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.238
It was kind of patchy

00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:44.950
and powdery feeling on the lips.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.350
But as a blush, I love it.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.330
This orange shade is so fun.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.650
I've seen these Glisten
split cake liners before,

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.180
but I've never tried them out.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.688
They released this limited-edition

00:00:53.688 --> 00:00:54.746
rainbow Pride Liner,

00:00:54.746 --> 00:00:56.796
and 100% of the profits are going

00:00:56.796 --> 00:01:00.360
to LGBTQIA+ charities,
which is incredible.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.260
This was kind of
intimidating to use at first.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:06.715
I'm not great at, like,
cool eyeliner looks,

00:01:06.715 --> 00:01:09.030
but this did make me want
to experiment a little.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.080
The colors are so, so pigmented.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.018
The one that did give me
a little bit of trouble

00:01:14.018 --> 00:01:14.851
was the yellow.

00:01:14.851 --> 00:01:16.773
I think I applied it with too much water,

00:01:16.773 --> 00:01:17.880
and it got a little patchy,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.360
but I think I fixed it.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.580
And the liners dry down super quickly.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.762
I'm not going to make a habit

00:01:22.762 --> 00:01:24.610
of featuring limited-edition stuff,

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.580
but this one felt too
special to not include.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.900
Also, this is probably
going to last me forever,

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.120
so I feel like it's totally worth it.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.210
I saw a TikTok of someone trying out

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.710
this Charlotte Tilbury liner,

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:36.835
and it made their eyes look

00:01:36.835 --> 00:01:38.601
so gorgeous and sparkly,

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:39.930
so I needed to try it.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.340
The black side worked fine,

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.973
but this metallic gold side

00:01:42.973 --> 00:01:44.640
is what I'm obsessed with.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.890
It went on my waterline super smoothly,

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.280
which hasn't really been my experience

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.800
with other pencil liners.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.280
I have an unusually wet waterline,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.900
so no eyeliner ever sticks to it,

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.100
but this one went on so easily.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.375
I feel like I can definitely

00:01:59.375 --> 00:02:00.841
see a bit of difference in the eye

00:02:00.841 --> 00:02:03.340
with the gold liner versus without it.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.840
It really does reflect the light

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.898
right onto your eye,

00:02:05.898 --> 00:02:07.480
so you have, like, these sparkly,

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.400
beautiful Disney princess eyes.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.360
I think this is a new favorite for me.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.290
Skin tints are still going
strong in beauty right now.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.660
This one is from Huda
Beauty's new GloWish line.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.060
I thought that I wouldn't like this,

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.380
but the second I blended
it in, I was obsessed.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:25.352
This gives your skin the most amazing glow

00:02:25.352 --> 00:02:27.810
and looks like you have
no foundation on at all.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.330
The glow isn't the most
natural-looking sheen,

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.400
but I still think it looked amazing.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.870
This is low coverage.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.280
It didn't cover up any of
my dark spots super well,

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.300
but it did a good job of
evening out my skin tone.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.800
I do think this is pretty
overpriced, though.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.750
$37 for a skin tint?
That just feels wrong.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.120
Phytosurgence is a new brand for me.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.890
I recently saw this
blush balm on Instagram,

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.081
and it's supposed to be like

00:02:53.081 --> 00:02:55.398
skin care and makeup in one.

00:02:55.398 --> 00:02:57.260
It has meadowfoam seed oil in it,

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.180
which is supposed to
be super moisturizing,

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.090
and it also has kokum butter,

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.332
which will soften the skin

00:03:02.332 --> 00:03:04.010
without clogging your pores.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.890
I was nervous about putting
this on over my foundation,

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.880
but it actually applied nicely.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.648
The texture is more moussey than balmy,

00:03:11.648 --> 00:03:12.650
which is interesting.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.791
It's super pigmented,

00:03:13.791 --> 00:03:15.470
so I didn't have to use too much.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:16.561
I think I messed up

00:03:16.561 --> 00:03:18.769
by going over the blush with a sponge,

00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:20.890
because I removed a
small patch of foundation

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:21.790
when I did that.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:24.015
I think using a brush
and just leaving it alone

00:03:24.015 --> 00:03:25.772
is probably the best
way to work with this,

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.605
but I still really, really like it.

00:03:27.605 --> 00:03:30.713
And this does dry down to
a soft, powdery finish.

